<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 18-JUN.</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 18-JUN.</headline>
<text>
<p>Typhoon Opal is a major threat to shipping south of Japan in the Philippine Sea at this time. Opal has top winds near 105 mph and is near 21.4n/133.6e, moving north at 15 mph. Top winds are expected to increase to 130 mph. The storm will continue northward and is expected to make landfall in Shikoku, Japan, in about 48 hours, with high winds, a damaging coastal storm surge, and flooding rains.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.  </p>
<p>There are no further statements at this time.</p>
